<%# The open conversation on the two-pane messaging page (`config.inbox_layout
    = :split`), inside the page's `chats_conversation` frame: the header
    (chats/conversations/_thread_header) over the shared thread body
    (chats/conversations/_thread, the same one the thread page and a dock
    window render).

    The thread is wrapped in a data-turbo-permanent element keyed by the
    conversation, the way the dock keys its own element: the inbox's live
    updates are Turbo 8 page refreshes that MORPH this whole page, and a
    morph leaves a permanent element alone, so the draft, the scroll
    position, the read state and the thread's stream subscription all go
    on untouched while the list beside it re-renders. Opening another
    conversation renders another id, which replaces it. The id also names
    the viewer: a visit that lands on another account's page (signing out
    and in, an account switcher) never inherits someone else's thread.

    The header stays outside it, so a refresh still brings it up to date
    (a mute, a renamed group).

    data-read: the server read the conversation as it rendered this (a row
    clicked); chats--split then clears its row's unread count at once,
    instead of when the list next refreshes. A pane rendered unread clears
    it when its thread reads (the thread's chats:read event).

    Locals: conversation, participant, messages, more, first_unread_id,
    counterpart, read_pending (as in chats/conversations/_thread). %>
<% title_id = dom_id(conversation, :title) %>
<%= tag.section class: "chats-split__pane", "aria-labelledby": title_id,
                data: { conversation_id: conversation.id, path: conversation_path(conversation),
                        read: !read_pending } do %>
  <%= render "chats/conversations/thread_header",
             conversation: conversation, participant: participant, counterpart: counterpart,
             heading: :h2, title_id: title_id, back_path: conversations_path(**chats_inbox_filter) %>

  <%= tag.div id: "chats_conversation_pane_#{conversation.id}_#{Chats.messager_key(chats_current_messager)}",
              class: "chats-split__thread", data: { turbo_permanent: true } do %>
    <%= render layout: "chats/conversations/thread",
               locals: {
                 conversation: conversation,
                 messages: messages,
                 more: more,
                 first_unread_id: first_unread_id,
                 counterpart: counterpart,
                 pane: true,
                 read_pending: read_pending
               } do %><% end %>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
